.TH audiocfg 1 "@PROJECT_YEAR@" "@PROJECT_VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
audiocfg \- configure PulseAudio devices and profiles
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B audiocfg
.RI [ OPTION ]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B audiocfg
connects to the PulseAudio server and lists audio endpoints or changes
card profiles. Profiles apply to hardware cards; use
.BR \-\-device
with a card name or index, or with a sink or source on that card.
.PP
Playback sinks and capture sources are listed with
.BR \-\-list .
Available card profiles (active profile marked with
.BR \(lq * \(rq)
are listed with
.BR \-\-list\-profiles .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-list
List playback and capture devices. Each line shows the kind, index,
PulseAudio name, human-readable description, and parent card index.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-device=\fIDEVICE\fR
Select a device for profile operations. \fIDEVICE\fR may be a card index
or name, or a sink or source index or name on that card.
.TP
.BR \-L ", " \-\-list\-profiles
List card profiles. Without
.BR \-\-device ,
profiles for every card are shown. With
.BR \-\-device ,
only the matching card is shown.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-profile=\fIPROFILE\fR
Set the active profile on the card selected with
.BR \-\-device .
Both options are required for this action.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-toggle=\fIPROFILES\fR
Cycle to the next profile on the card given by
.BR \-\-device .
\fIPROFILES\fR is a comma-separated list of profile names; if the active
profile is the last in the list, the first profile is selected. If the active
profile is not in the list, the first profile is selected.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Increase logging verbosity (may be repeated).
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Decrease logging verbosity.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit successfully.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print version and license information and exit successfully.
.SH EXAMPLES
List devices:
.RS
.B audiocfg \-\-list
.RE
List profiles for one card:
.RS
.B audiocfg \-\-list\-profiles \-\-device 0
.RE
Switch a card to an HDMI stereo profile:
.RS
.B audiocfg \-\-device alsa_card.pci\-0000_00_1f.3 \-\-profile output:hdmi\-stereo
.RE
Cycle through a fixed set of profiles:
.RS
.B audiocfg \-\-device playback:48 \-\-toggle output:hdmi\-stereo,off,output:hdmi\-surround
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
An error occurred (invalid options, PulseAudio connection failure, unknown
device, or profile change failure).
